    "value": "| Req ID | Area | Requirement | Epic  Where it will be covered | Covered in a user story? Or SFCC OOTB/code-base | What's needed to progress |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| DMU-001 | Data Migration | The system will receive all active product records via the AP21 to SFCC product feed through MuleSoft, including product names, descriptions, attributes, imagery references and category assignments, covering approximately 1,600 active SKUs at any point in time |  |  |  |\n| DMU-002 | Data Migration | The system will consume ongoing product data synchronisation into SFCC via MuleSoft, treating the downstream systems as the authoritative source of record for all product data post-migration. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-003 | Data Migration | The system will preserve multi-region product catalogue assignments and regional merchandising configurations across all storefronts. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-004 | Data Migration | The system will migrate customer email address and Omneo ID only. All other customer data including name, phone number, saved delivery addresses and communication preferences will be sourced live from Omneo at login. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-005 | Data Migration | The system will not migrate customer passwords; customers will be required to reset their password on first login to the new platform. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-006 | Data Migration | The system will not migrate saved payment card details; customers will be required to re-enter payment information at next purchase after go-live. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-007 | Data Migration | The system will not migrate historical order records into SFCC; order history will be accessible via Mulesoft where customer identifiers match across online and in-store channels. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-008 | Data Migration | The system will display online orders only in the My Account order history for the Middle East storefront; offline and retail orders will not be surfaced. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-009 | Data Migration | The system will reconfigure existing Contentful API connections to point to the new commerce platform; no bulk content re-entry will be required for content already managed in Contentful. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-011 | Data Migration | The system will support a snapshot and delta migration approach: an initial bulk data export followed by one or more delta migrations based on timestamps, and a final delta run close to DNS cutover to minimise data gaps. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-012 | Data Migration | The system will be supported by repeatable migration scripts capable of executing multiple delta runs; one-off scripts that cannot be re-executed will not be acceptable. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-013 | URL Strategy | The system will preserve the existing storefront locale prefix conventions: AU (root, no prefix), US (/us/), UK (/uk/), EU (/en-eu/, /fr-eu/, /es-eu/, /it-eu/), HK (/hk/), ME (/en-ae/), and ROW (/en-ch/, /en-ca/). |  |  |  |\n| DMU-014 | URL Strategy | The system will update category URLs to support SEO consolidation and reduce category cannibalisation (e.g. a canonical path such as /clothing/dresses), with 301 redirects applied from all legacy category URLs. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-015 | URL Strategy | The system will preserve the existing product URL format including the .html suffix (e.g. /alchemy-ruffle-mini-dress-blue-poppy.html) to maintain existing indexed URLs and avoid unnecessary 301 overhead. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-016 | URL Strategy | The system will configure the AU storefront as the root domain with no locale prefix and designate it as the x-default hreflang target. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-018 | URL Strategy | The system will implement 301 permanent redirects for all URLs that change as a result of the platform migration, covering product, category, content, and asset pages. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-019 | URL Strategy | The system will implement all URL redirects as defined in the redirect mapping document, which will be produced during the build phase and validated prior to go-live. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-020 | URL Strategy | The system will manage all 301 redirects at the CDN or edge level to minimise performance impact on the application layer. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-021 | URL Strategy | The system will preserve all existing CDN redirect rules and SEO configuration from the current Cloudflare setup, carrying them forward to the new platform CDN during migration. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-022 | SEO | The system will output canonical tags on all indexable pages, referencing the preferred URL for that storefront. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-562](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-562) — Canonical Tags on All Indexable Pages | No canonical mechanism exists today — full custom build. Now also covers DMU-023 (SFCC-563 merged in 2026-09-14). See comments on SFCC-562. |\n| DMU-023 | SEO | The system will apply canonical tags on all filtered and faceted PLP URLs pointing back to the unfiltered base PLP URL to prevent duplicate content indexation. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-562](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-562) — Canonical Tags on All Indexable Pages (SFCC-563 merged in, 2026-09-14) | Blanket canonical-to-base risks suppressing facet pages with real search demand (e.g. \\\"blue dresses\\\"). Merged into SFCC-562 (was SFCC-563) — need Tell No Lies/Sparro to confirm which facet combos should stay indexable, everything else defaults to canonical. |\n| DMU-024 | SEO | The system will apply hreflang tags only on canonical PDP URLs; non-canonical URL variants will not carry hreflang tags, and canonical tags will be retained on all PDP URL variants. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-564](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-564) — Hreflang Tags on Canonical PDP URLs & XML Sitemap (covers DMU-024 + DMU-025) | DMU-024 (HTML tags) and DMU-025 (sitemap) ask for two separate hreflang methods — Google recommends picking one, not mixing. Recommend sitemap-only; see comment on SFCC-564. Reciprocal locale linking also needs adding as an explicit acceptance criterion. |\n| DMU-025 | SEO | The system will implement hreflang tags on all pages via XML sitemap format, mapping all locale codes to their respective storefront URLs. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-564](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-564) — Hreflang Tags on Canonical PDP URLs & XML Sitemap (covers DMU-024 + DMU-025) | See comment on SFCC-564 — recommend this becomes the single hreflang method (sitemap-only), replacing DMU-024's HTML tags rather than running alongside them. Needs reciprocal locale linking as an explicit acceptance criterion. |\n| DMU-026 | SEO | The system will consolidate hreflang tags from the current 200+ country-specific tags to approximately 12 regional and language-level tags, to be confirmed with the Sparro SEO team prior to implementation. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-565](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-565) — Hreflang Consolidation (~12 Regional/Language Tags) | Hreflang strategy to be confirmed with Sparro SEO team. Also flagged on SFCC-565 — our current en-eu/uk style URL slugs aren't valid ISO hreflang codes (Google explicitly ignores \\\"EU\\\" and \\\"UK\\\"), so the final ~12 codes need to be real ISO language-country pairs, not the routing slugs reused. |\n| DMU-027 | SEO | The system will automatically generate and serve XML sitemaps per storefront and locale, refreshed on a scheduled daily basis. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-566](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-566) — XML Sitemap Generation per Storefront & Locale (covers DMU-027/028/029/030) | BM Sitemaps + Job Scheduler give scheduled generation OOTB — still needs a CDN routing decision to expose it on the storefront domain. See comment on SFCC-566. |\n| DMU-028 | SEO | The system will exclude disabled and deleted pages from all XML sitemaps upon regeneration. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-566](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-566) — XML Sitemap Generation per Storefront & Locale (covers DMU-027/028/029/030) | Automatic OOTB behaviour of the BM sitemap job — nothing to build. See comment on SFCC-566. |\n| DMU-029 | SEO | The system will ensure homepage URLs in XML sitemaps include a trailing slash. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-566](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-566) — XML Sitemap Generation per Storefront & Locale (covers DMU-027/028/029/030) | Needs a static URL added via BM's Sitemap Configuration screen. See comment on SFCC-566. |\n| DMU-030 | SEO | The system will ensure that all URLs blocked in robots.txt do not appear in any XML sitemap. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-566](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-566) — XML Sitemap Generation per Storefront & Locale (covers DMU-027/028/029/030) | Self-satisfying once robots.txt + sitemap exist — a QA check at go-live, not a build item. See comment on SFCC-566. |\n| DMU-031 | SEO | The system will render all product, category, and content pages server-side (SSR) to ensure full crawlability by search engines and AI bots without dependence on client-side JavaScript execution. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-567](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-567) — Server-Side Rendering (SSR) for All Crawlable Pages | Already true — PWA Kit is SSR by default. Sign-off only. See comment on SFCC-567. |\n| DMU-032 | SEO | The system will generate unique, human-readable title tags per page following the existing format: [Product Name] [Colour] | Zimmermann, configurable via Business Manager meta tag rules. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-568](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-568) — Title Tag Generation (All Page Templates) | Mostly OOTB via BM Page Meta Tag Rules; homepage still hardcoded placeholder text. See comment on SFCC-568. |\n| DMU-033 | SEO | The system will generate unique meta description tags per product and category page, sourced from product and catalogue data in SFCC. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-569](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-569) — Meta Description Tags (PDP & PLP) | Same BM mechanism as title tags; same homepage gap. See comment on SFCC-569. |\n| DMU-034 | SEO | The system will implement a single H1 tag per page template across homepage, PLP, and PDP, with correct H2–H6 heading hierarchy and no duplicate heading tags. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-570](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-570) — Heading Hierarchy (H1–H6) Across Page Templates | PLP renders two H1s side by side (category name + product count) — base template bug, needs fixing as part of this story. See comment on SFCC-570. |\n| DMU-035 | SEO | The system will include the product colour within the H1 tag on all PDP pages. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-570](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-570) — Heading Hierarchy (H1–H6) Across Page Templates | PDP H1 is currently a hardcoded placeholder with no product name/colour — needs rework. See comment on SFCC-570. |\n| DMU-036 | SEO | The system will provide a CMS-editable on-page SEO content field on all category and PLP pages, configurable at individual storefront level. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-577](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-577) — PLP SEO Copy Content Field (CMS-Editable, BM-Configurable) | No PLP override or Contentful wiring exists yet — net-new build. See comment on SFCC-577. |\n| DMU-037 | SEO | The system will serve a robots.txt file that permits crawling of all indexable pages including the bag page, and restricts crawling of checkout flow steps, account pages, search result pages, and filtered URL parameters. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-571](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-571) — robots.txt Configuration | Current robots.txt blocks nothing — needs the disallow rules added. See comment on SFCC-571. |\n| DMU-038 | SEO | The system will implement Product and Merchant Listing Schema on all PDPs per the schema template provided by the Tell No Lies SEO team. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-572](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-572) — Product & Merchant Listing Structured Data Schema (PDP) (covers DMU-038 + DMU-042) | Schema template to be provided by Tell No Lies. No JSON-LD exists anywhere yet — clean build once it lands. See comment on SFCC-572. |\n| DMU-039 | SEO | The system will implement CollectionPage, BreadcrumbList, and ItemList Schema on all PLP pages per the Sparro SEO team schema template. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-573](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-573) — CollectionPage, BreadcrumbList & ItemList Schema (PLP) | Schema template to be provided by Sparro. Same zero-JSON-LD start; can reuse existing breadcrumb data once built. See comment on SFCC-573. |\n| DMU-040 | SEO | The system will implement LocalBusiness Schema on all individual boutique location detail pages per the Sparro SEO team schema template. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-574](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-574) — LocalBusiness Schema (Boutique Location Detail Pages) | Schema template to be provided by Sparro. No individual boutique page exists yet — needs building before schema can attach. See comment on SFCC-574. |\n| DMU-041 | SEO | The system will implement Organisation Schema on each regional storefront homepage per the Sparro SEO team schema template, with url and contactPoint fields configured per storefront. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-575](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-575) — Organisation Schema (Regional Storefront Homepages) | Schema template to be provided by Sparro. Real blocker is content (logo/social/contact details), not code — see comment on SFCC-575, also flags a question on whether this needs to appear on boutique pages too. |\n| DMU-042 | SEO | The system will implement structured data for products to include available sizes and per-offer availability, driven by real-time inventory data. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-572](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-572) — Product & Merchant Listing Structured Data Schema (PDP) (covers DMU-038 + DMU-042) | Additive to DMU-038 — real-time inventory data is already wired into the PDP today. See comment on SFCC-572. |\n| DMU-043 | GEO | The system will deliver the technical foundations required for post-launch GEO enablement — including SSR, structured data, canonical URLs, and XML sitemaps — ensuring no architectural decisions block future GEO activation. | SFCC-22 (SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing) | [SFCC-576](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-576) — GEO Technical Foundations Readiness Check | Sign-off story rolling up SSR/canonical/sitemap/schema status — see comment on SFCC-576 for where each piece stands. |\n| DMU-044 | Data Migration | The system will migrate customer wishlist data from Magento, mapping wishlist items to the corresponding SFCC product records and associating them with the migrated customer account via Omneo ID. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-045 | Data Migration | The system will migrate product enrichment data currently maintained in Magento to SFCC, including badges, category assignments, colour swatches, colour grouping, swatch images and Shop the Look associations, mapped to the corresponding SFCC product and catalogue structure. |  |  |  |\n| DMU-046 | Data Migration | The system will migrate active Notify Me subscriptions from Magento to SFCC, carrying forward customer email addresses and product IDs and mapping them to the corresponding SFCC product records. |  |  |  |\n| AAB-001 | Tag Management & Data Layer | The system must load the GTM container on all storefront pages across all regional sites. |  |  |  |\n| AAB-002 | Tag Management & Data Layer | The system must populate a well-structured data layer that serves as the single source of truth for all downstream analytics and marketing tags, built natively in SFCC and covering all required customer and product interactions across the full shopping journey. |  |  |  |\n| AAB-003 | Cookies & Consent Management | The system must consistently populate the data layer with all commerce and analytics events regardless of consent state. Didomi, operating at the tag layer, will gate advertising and personalisation tags so they only fire after the visitor has explicitly accepted. |  |  |  |\n| AAB-004 | A/B Testing | The system will ensure the data layer populated in AAB-002 includes the attributes required for Optimizely audience segmentation - such as authenticated state, customer group, loyalty status, storefront region, new vs returning visitor and device type. |  |  | Requirement needs updating per Tell No Lies: Optimizely is outside GTM, needs separate frontend tag in PWA Kit page head. US only. |\n| AAB-005 | Heatmapping & Session Replay | The system will ensure the data layer populated in AAB-002 includes page type, authenticated state and storefront region to support Crazy Egg segmentation and suppression configuration. |  |  | Requirement needs updating per Tell No Lies: Crazy Egg is outside GTM, needs separate frontend tag in PWA Kit page head. |"
  }
}"}

{"result":"{
