    "body": "One thing worth flagging on DMU-022/DMU-023 before these go further - SFCC-562 and SFCC-563 (the two canonical tag stories) are really the same piece of work split in two. 562 is \"output a canonical tag on every indexable page\" and 563 is \"except for filtered PLP URLs, point the canonical somewhere else instead\" - same underlying logic, just one extra branch for the filter case. 563 already declares it depends on 562, which is usually a sign these should just be one story rather than two with a hard sequencing dependency between them.\n\nRecommend merging 563 into 562 - one story covering both the general case and the filtered-PLP case (including the BM-configurability note from 563 about letting merchandisers override the canonical on specific filter pages).\n\nWorth noting SFCC-564 (hreflang) isn't part of this overlap - it uses canonical PDP URLs as a target, it doesn't generate canonical tags itself, so it's genuinely separate work. It should just get an explicit \"depends on SFCC-562\" link added, since right now that dependency exists in practice but isn't declared anywhere.",
